WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.380
In a process with a fixed rule, the state is everything

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:05.490
you need to work out the next step.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.630
The same state must lead to the same next state.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.180
So once a state repeats, the whole path

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:12.310
repeats from there.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.210
Finding the state is the key to long-run questions.

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.390
Questions about the hundredth or thousandth

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:19.440
step look impossible.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:23.230
But if the states repeat in a short cycle, you only need

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:25.060
the position inside the cycle.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:26.790
Start with three.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.400
Each time, double the number and keep only

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.310
its last digit.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.650
The list begins three, six, two, four, eight, six.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.550
What is the fiftieth number?

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:38.390
Pause and look for a repeat.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.650
After the first number, the list repeats six,

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.080
two, four, eight.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:48.720
Notice that three itself never comes back.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:52.000
The cycle starts at the second number, not the first.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.120
From the second number to the fiftieth there

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.390
are forty-nine numbers.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.030
Forty-nine is twelve complete cycles and one more.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:03.790
So the fiftieth number is the first in the cycle: six.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.550
Sometimes one number is not enough to be the state.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:10.760
If each number is the last digit of the sum of the

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:13.620
previous two, then seeing a one does not tell you

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:14.530
what comes next.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:16.810
You need the last two numbers.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:18.330
The state is a pair.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:22.190
In the same way, if a robot may not reverse its last

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:25.020
move, its position alone is not the state.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.180
You must also remember which way it just moved.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:30.740
Remember enough to know what can happen next,

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:31.740
and no more.

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:34.000
Decide what the state is.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.060
Find where a state first repeats.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.730
Then use a remainder to locate the position

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:39.500
in the cycle.

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:42.370
Notebook challenge: start with seven as

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:43.180
the first number.

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:46.550
To get each next number, triple the current one and keep

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:47.800
only the last digit.

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:49.760
What is the thirtieth number?
